 "title": "How to Sell Different Products",
 "topic": "sales",
 "summary": "The creator suggests adjusting your sales angle based on the type of product you are selling. Different strategies should be used for cheap items, expensive items, unknown brands, common products, gifts, and items people already own.",
 "key_points": [
  "If selling something cheap, sell the 'why I didn't know this existed' angle.",
  "If selling something expensive, compare it to something even more expensive or something dumb.",
  "If selling an unknown brand that nobody has heard of, sell it like a secret.",
  "If selling what everybody else is selling, sell the deal.",
  "If selling a gift, sell to the person paying for it, not the person getting it.",
  "If selling something everybody already owns, sell the upgrade.",
  "If you sell every product the same way, you will end up selling none of them."
 ],
 "content": "how to sell different products #tiktokshop If you're selling cheap, why I didn't know this existed. If you're selling expensive, compare it to something even more expensive or something dumb. If you're selling an unknown brand nobody's heard of, sell it like a secret. If you're selling what everybody else is selling, sell the deal. If you're selling a gift, sell to the person paying it, not the person getting it. If you're selling something everybody already owns, sell the upgrade. If you sell every product the same way, you'll end up selling none of them.",
